      "content": "While pests aren't the primary culprits, certain soil microbes can inadvertently tie up nutrients deeper in the ground, making them unavailable to your grass roots. In wet Portland soil, fungal infections like take-all root rot are often more friendly to these microorganisms and physically degrade grass roots, causing that exact stunted, yellow look you're seeing. Focusing on soil health through aeration and pH balance will help your grass access whatever remaining nutrients are already present.",
